## One suggestion I'd add

Since you're doing this as both a useful tool and a learning project, I would adopt a simple rule from the beginning:

> **Every phase should end with a usable application.**

That means after Phase 1, you should already be able to run `python ...`, open `/gm` and `/player`, and see *something* happen. Even if it's just changing "Hello Adventurers!" to "Welcome to the Dungeon!", each phase leaves the project in a working, demonstrable state. That tends to keep momentum high and makes the project enjoyable to return to over time.
